{"id": "q_longmont_session_12_council_chamber_roster", "question": "Who's actually in the council chamber for the Session 12 fight with the Wolf?", "answer": "TL;DR: The council chamber fight in Session 12 includes **Bonogo**, **the Wolf (target of the chase/attack)**, **Council members**, and **Elite Corrupted Guards (including reinforcements emerging from behind the banners)**.\n\nHere’s what’s grounded in the projection:\n\n- **Bonogo (OBSERVED)**: Actively “chasing/attacking Wolf” and “dealing major damage to Wolf,” including attacking from behind—so he is definitively in the chamber during the fight.\n- **Elite Corrupted Guards (OBSERVED)**: Present in the chamber, with “3–4 additional corrupted elite guards… revealed by hidden doors behind council banners,” and acting as active opponents/reinforcements.\n- **Council (OBSERVED + CANON)**: Located in the “Council Chamber,” engaged in an active, tense meeting. Since the fight occurs there, council members are physically present unless removed (no evidence they were).\n- **The Wolf**: Not a full entity entry here, but directly referenced as the target Bonogo is attacking in this scene, so it is present.\n\nNo explicit evidence places **Torbin Jove** or regular **City Guard** inside the chamber during this specific fight.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Location: Council Chamber (central, warded, with hidden passages behind banners)\n- Defenses: Arcane locks, magical wards\n- Active threats: Elite Corrupted Guards (reinforcements), The Wolf\n- Noncombatants: Council members under pressure and tension", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 92, "top_5": [["ent_council", 2.2944], ["ent_the_wolf", 1.8456], ["ent_secret_escape_tunnel", 1.8], ["ent_eirik", 1.6856], ["ent_magic_pulse_alarms", 1.6344]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_council", "ent_the_wolf", "ent_secret_escape_tunnel", "ent_eirik", "ent_magic_pulse_alarms", "ent_amulets_of_co