{"id": "q_longmont_campaign_general_notes_1", "question": "Who are the Shepherds, and what god or power do they answer to?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Shepherds are human cult leaders and recruiters—part of the Shepherds’ Flock—who serve and advance the will of Maelthor, an otherworldly entity promising ascension and seeking to emerge into the world.\n\nThe **Shepherds** are not a separate religion—they are the driving figures within **the cult (The Shepherd’s Flock)**.  \n- CANON: They are **mostly disillusioned humans** (veterans, laborers, apprentices) who have become **fanatical leaders and recruiters**.  \n- CANON/OBSERVED: A “Shepherd” can also refer to a central figure described as a **“godling made flesh,” not yet risen**, suggesting a transformation or embodiment tied to their power.  \n- OBSERVED: They manipulate, recruit, and justify atrocities (burnings, sacrifice) as necessary for a “greater good,” often under a **benevolent guise**.\n\nThey answer to **Maelthor**:  \n- CANON: The cult explicitly believes **“The Shepherds are followers of Maelthor.”**  \n- CANON: Maelthor is an **ancient, otherworldly power** promising **ascension and transcendence** to those who help awaken it.  \n- OBSERVED: Their actions are meant to **feed Maelthor’s strength** and hasten its emergence.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Demographics: Mostly disillusioned humans (CANON)  \n- Role: Cult leaders, recruiters, manipulators (CANON/OBSERVED)  \n- Alignment: Fanatically devoted to Maelthor; justify sacrifice and destruction (OBSERVED)  \n- Power Source: Maelthor—an otherworldly entity seeking awakening (CANON)  \n- Structure: Operate within the Shepherd’s Flock (the cult) (CANON)", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 106, "top_5": [["ent_shepherd", 2.0442], ["ent_seren_darkroot", 1.8], ["ent_great_shepherd", 1.7517], ["ent_sing_enough_times_and_something_will_answer", 1.3641], ["ent_human_refugees