{"id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_2", "question": "What does the council room itself throw at us that screws with the fight?", "answer": "TL;DR: The council chamber fights back mainly through its **magical defenses (wards, arcane locks)** and **layout (sealed exits, circular space, escape tunnel)**, plus **social/mechanical pressure** that can disrupt player actions mid-combat.\n\nThe room itself isn’t described as spawning hazards like traps or creatures, but it absolutely interferes:\n\n- **Magical defenses / ancient wards (OBSERVED – Council.defenses):** These can plausibly activate during conflict, restricting movement, blocking attacks, or protecting council members. This is the strongest “the room hits back” element.\n- **Arcane locks on doors (OBSERVED – Council.defenses):** Exits can seal mid-fight, trapping players or splitting the party.\n- **Secret escape tunnel (OBSERVED – Council.relationship_tags):** Creates shifting positioning—NPCs may vanish or reappear, complicating targeting and control.\n- **Large circular chamber (OBSERVED – Council.governance/geography):** Open sightlines + central exposure make it hard to take cover or control angles.\n- **Parchment birds (OBSERVED – Council.relationship_tags):** მოძრable/message-carrying elements that can interfere with visibility, communication, or spell targeting (indirect disruption).\n- **Time pressure & divided council (CANON – Council.atmosphere/operational_status):** Mechanics and tension actively “screw with the fight” by forcing rushed decisions and split priorities.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: magical wards, arcane locks\n- Geography: large circular chamber, central location\n- Features: secret escape tunnel, parchment birds\n- Atmosphere: high tension, time pressure affecting actions", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 103, "top_5": [["ent_council", 2.0992], ["ent_room", 1.8717], ["ent_amu