{"id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_4_v2", "question": "If the council keeps talking and doesn't act, what bites us?", "answer": "TL;DR: If the Council stalls, the cult’s plan advances—tainted meat spreads, rituals continue, and you risk a **flesh kaiju emerging due to delayed or failed action**.\n\nThe biggest immediate threat (CANON + OBSERVED) is momentum: the **cultists** are actively working to “continue to the center and spill blood onto the meat,” and there is “real pressure… it’s already been distributed to places.” If no decisive action is taken, contamination spreads beyond containment.\n\nAt the same time, the Council’s own dynamics (CANON) make things worse: hesitation, possible **cult sympathizers**, and failure to reach the “required influence threshold” means repeated stalls while time pressure increases. That gives the cultists—who have **defensive spells and traps** and **reinforcements in tunnels**—time to fortify and expand.\n\nNet effect: what bites you is escalation on multiple fronts—wider corruption in the city, stronger enemy positions, and the looming catastrophic outcome explicitly flagged as **“flesh kaiju emerging due to delayed or failed action.”**\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Council:\n  - Operational Status: may stall if no plan reaches threshold; time pressure increases\n  - Loyalty Context: possible cult sympathizers; threat not universally accepted\n  - Goals: handle tainted meat; emergency response\n- Cultists:\n  - Goals: spill blood onto the meat; lure players; expand operations\n  - Defenses: spells and traps\n  - Demographics: multiple groups, reinforcements in tunnels\n  - Pressure: tainted meat already distributed", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 206, "top_5": [["ent_council", 1.862], ["ent_talking_spoon", 1.4672], ["ent_pippa", 1.4672], ["ent_compelled_to_act_alone", 1.398], ["ent_the_flying_gritspike", 1.398]], "selected_entity_i