{"id": "q_pre_post", "question": "Before vs after the council fight-how's the Wolf different?", "answer": "TL;DR: The projection does not describe any **before vs. after change** in the Wolf due to the council fight; only his ongoing influence and prior actions are established.\n\nBased on available facts, there is **no OBSERVED or CANON update** showing how the Wolf differs after the council fight. What we do know:\n\n- CANON (the cult history): *“The Wolf has been subtly leading key figures of the city guard into the cult’s fold.”*\n- OBSERVED (Mirathorn goals): the city *“was betrayed by Wolf.”*\n- OBSERVED (Mirathorn current_location): the city is under *“Wolf’s grip.”*\n\nThese indicate a **pre-existing state** where the Wolf is already exerting covert control and influence within Mirathorn, especially through the City Guard.\n\nHowever, there are **no facts describing a post-fight transformation, escalation, injury, exposure, or defeat** tied to the council encounter.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- History: Subtle corruption of City Guard leadership (CANON)\n- Influence: Ongoing control (“Wolf’s grip”) over Mirathorn (OBSERVED)\n- Actions: Betrayal of Mirathorn (OBSERVED)\n\nConclusion: The projection lacks any recorded “after” state—so mechanically and narratively, the Wolf is unchanged as far as current canon/observed data shows.", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 96, "top_5": [["ent_eirik", 2.2565], ["ent_the_wolf", 1.9365], ["The_Shepherd_s_Council", 1.7164], ["ent_city_guard", 1.6694], ["ent_council", 1.66]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_eirik", "ent_the_wolf", "The_Shepherd_s_Council", "ent_city_guard", "ent_council", "ent_secret_escape_tunnel", "ent_commander_thalia_ashenvale", "ent_mirathorn", "ent_wolf", "ent_key", "ent_the_fight", "ent_torbin_jove", "ent_the_cult", "ent_goblin", "ent_agricultural_district", "ent_amulet_of_council", "ent_amulets_of_council", "ent_b